  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAn upper level trough axis is directly overhead early this\nafternoon and will slowly shift eastward away from the area by\nthis evening. The presence of the cold pool aloft and moist,\ncyclonic flow has allowed for scattered rain showers to develop \nand these showers will continue through this afternoon before \ndiminishing this evening. Extra cloud cover and little to no\ninstability has prevented any thunderstorms from developing \nthus far. While an isolated rumble cannot be ruled out, overall \ncoverage looks very sparse so thunder was removed from the \nforecast for the remainder of the day. A brief period of \nmoderate rain could occur with some of the taller showers, but \nthese will not result in any hydrological impacts. As the trough\ndeparts and showers end tonight, partial clearing will likely \nallow for valley fog to form, some of which can become locally \ndense.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nAfter a dry day on Wednesday, another upper level disturbance\nand frontal system will cross the area Thursday into Friday. \nThis will bring another round of showers and thunderstorms\nacross the area. These showers may occur in a couple of rounds\nwith one earlier in the day into the afternoon from the Capital\nDistrict and points south and east with another round\napproaching from the west along the warm/occluded front later \nin the afternoon into the evening. If there are enough breaks in\nthe clouds, moderate instability present along with around 30 \nkt of shear could support a few stronger thunderstorms capable \nof wind damage. Most of the area is outlooked in a marginal risk\nfor severe thunderstorms for Thursday. Precipitable water \nvalues increasing to around 1.50 inches could support some brief\ndownpours as well. As the frontal system departs on Friday, some\nadditional showers and rumbles of thunder are possible as\nanother upper shortwave passes through the area, but the severe\nthreat on Friday is lower compared to Thursday.\n\nDrier weather looks to return for the upcoming weekend. \nTemperatures look to remain seasonable behind the cold front as \nwell.",
